00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:53.560
that poor and special needs children in particular have received inadequate instruction during the shutdown.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:59.360
This is a disgrace, it is a failure, it is going to cause huge economic problems and emotional problems

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:00.520
and learning problems.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:04.700
School districts around the country are weighing the needs of students against the danger

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:10.500
that in-person instruction could cause COVID-19 to spread within their communities and teachers unions

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:14.220
are understandably concerned about protecting the health of their members.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:19.500
But in Los Angeles the teachers union is exploiting the COVID-19 crisis to prevent competition

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.060
from charter schools.

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:25.480
The United Teachers Los Angeles co-signed a document with nine other unions

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:30.660
and the Democratic Socialists of America calling for a moratorium on all new charter schools

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:32.340
and private voucher programs.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:35.840
It's about protecting a monopoly from losing any students,

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:38.538
and the funding that goes along with those students.

00:01:38.538 --> 00:01:39.680
Corey DeAngelis is the director of school choice at Reason Foundation, the nonprofit

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:46.720
that publishes Reason TV, he says that entrenched interests are trying to stop families

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:48.091
